WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.048
Checks and balances for every call.

2
00:00:02.328 --> 00:00:04.760
Before you move on, fix one habit in place.

3
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:20.485
Every call your code makes should end with three checks: did the request succeed (exceptions handled, transient ones retried with a limit), did the model finish ( stop_reason is what you expected), and what did it cost (usage recorded with the request id).

4
00:00:20.765 --> 00:00:25.437
Those three lines are cheap, and they are what turns a demo into something you can operate.

5
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:33.205
The next lesson uses the usage numbers to compare models on cost and latency, and to decide which model a task deserves.
